{"assets":["/statement-assets/a1a1b3f617ce8e90df12c53001919a0f2a41231542e07d813ed8aa4c8e9b3521.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1091","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. New Year and the Sphere Transmission"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ people sitting in a circle, numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in the order in which they are seated. That is, for all $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n-1$$$, the people with id $$$i$$$ and $$$i+1$$$ are adjacent. People with id $$$n$$$ and $$$1$$$ are adjacent as well."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The person with id $$$1$$$ initially has a ball. He picks a positive integer $$$k$$$ at most $$$n$$$, and passes the ball to his $$$k$$$-th neighbour in the direction of increasing ids, that person passes the ball to his $$$k$$$-th neighbour in the same direction, and so on until the person with the id $$$1$$$ gets the ball back. When he gets it back, people do not pass the ball any more."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For instance, if $$$n = 6$$$ and $$$k = 4$$$, the ball is passed in order $$$[1, 5, 3, 1]$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the set of all people that touched the ball. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the game is the sum of the ids of people that touched it. In the above example, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" would be $$$1 + 5 + 3 = 9$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find and report the set of possible "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun values"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" for all choices of positive integer $$$k$$$. It can be shown that under the constraints of the problem, the ball always gets back to the $$$1$$$-st player after finitely many steps, and there are no more than $$$10^5$$$ possible "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun values"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" for given $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line consists of a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 10^9$$$) — the number of people playing with the ball."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose the set of all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun values"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$f_1, f_2, \\dots, f_m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single line containing $$$m$$$ space separated integers $$$f_1$$$ through $$$f_m$$$ in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"increasing"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 5 9 21\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n16\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 10 28 64 136\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, we've already shown that picking $$$k = 4$$$ yields "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$9$$$, as does $$$k = 2$$$. Picking $$$k = 6$$$ results in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$1$$$. For $$$k = 3$$$ we get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fun value"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$5$$$ and with $$$k = 1$$$ or $$$k = 5$$$ we get $$$21$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a1a1b3f617ce8e90df12c53001919a0f2a41231542e07d813ed8aa4c8e9b3521.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, the values $$$1$$$, $$$10$$$, $$$28$$$, $$$64$$$ and $$$136$$$ are achieved for instance for $$$k = 16$$$, $$$8$$$, $$$4$$$, $$$10$$$ and $$$11$$$, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1091C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1091/problem/C"}